\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {36}{\ignorespaces Laptop functional diagnostics only, not performance evidence. No cross-store acknowledgement comparison. Local structure test: transcribed from the audit report; raw samples not retained. Each cell lists IEEE run 1; run 2 separately; -- means not measured. Fresh mapping, \texttt  {MAP\_POPULATE}, write-prefault, \texttt  {pwrite} and anonymous memory have no per-put foreground persistence guarantee. Write-prefault writes every page and data-syncs before timing; \texttt  {MAP\_POPULATE} is not that control. Data sync means per-put \texttt  {fdatasync}; grouped sync is a covered-ticket model. Neither is the engine's complete file-and-directory barrier. Finite-case rates are not capacity estimates; per-call occupancy cannot be checked without retained samples. Source and run labels are in \texttt  {local-structure-test.csv}.}}{33}{table.caption.53}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:local-structure}{{36}{33}{Laptop functional diagnostics only, not performance evidence. No cross-store acknowledgement comparison. Local structure test: transcribed from the audit report; raw samples not retained. Each cell lists IEEE run 1; run 2 separately; -- means not measured. Fresh mapping, \texttt {MAP\_POPULATE}, write-prefault, \texttt {pwrite} and anonymous memory have no per-put foreground persistence guarantee. Write-prefault writes every page and data-syncs before timing; \texttt {MAP\_POPULATE} is not that control. Data sync means per-put \texttt {fdatasync}; grouped sync is a covered-ticket model. Neither is the engine's complete file-and-directory barrier. Finite-case rates are not capacity estimates; per-call occupancy cannot be checked without retained samples. Source and run labels are in \texttt {local-structure-test.csv}}{table.caption.53}{}}
